#NEXUS

[ poole2022a_fig9: Iguanodontian MCC tree with pies on every node, read with the image as it stands (root at left). Pies often touch or overlap and several stretches run two parallel verticals side by side (Shishugou taxon/Clypeodonta, Uteodon/Camptosaurus/Styracosterna, the hadrosauroid ladder); every node was checked against the paper's Fig. 8, the same MCC tree drawn without pies, and against its text ('Uteodon is the most basal ankylopollexian', 'Camptosaurus is recovered as the sister to Styracosterna'). Printed clade names kept as internal labels: Neornithischia, Clypeodonta, Hypsilophodontidae, Thescelosauridae, Iguanodontia, Rhabdodontoidea, Rhabdodontidae, Dryomorpha, Dryosauridae, Ankylopollexia, Styracosterna, Iguanodontidae, Hadrosauroidea; 'Unnamed node' (an arrow to the Barilium-Jinzhousaurus clade) is not a name and is left out. Picked case (pie charts on nodes; not a sample, not for accuracy estimates). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only; the pies, bars and support values are not encoded. 68 tips, 0 polytomies; 13 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. ]

